  "body": " Subplot Updated Code   Here is an interactive code box that functions identically to the MATLAB command window.  %% Chapter 11 Follow Along Work % Define the force vector force = 0:5000:40000; % Define the length vector len = [25,27,29,31.1,32.9,35,37,39,40.8]\/1000; %Calculate area based off information area = pi*0.005^2; len_0 = 0.025; %inital length %Calculate stress and strain according to equations e_stress = force \/ area; e_strain = (len-len_0)\/len_0; % plot (e_strain, e_stress) % orginal plot command % plot (e_strain, e_stress, 'g') % plot a green line % plot (e_strain, e_stress, 'mp--') % plot magenta pentagrams (dashed line) % plot (e_strain, e_stress, 'k<-.') % plot black left arrows (dashdot line) % plot(e_strain,e_stress,'mp--'); % plot magenta pentagrams (dashed line) %hold on %plot(e_strain_teflon,e_stress_teflon,'g*--'); %any number of plotting commands can go here% %hold off subplot (2,3,1) plot (e_strain, e_stress, 'mp--') subplot (2,3,2) plot (e_strain, e_stress, 'cp--') subplot (2,3,3) plot (e_strain, e_stress, 'kp--') subplot (2,3,4) plot (e_strain, e_stress, 'g*--') subplot (2,3,5) plot (e_strain, e_stress, 'r*--') subplot (2,3,6) plot (e_strain, e_stress, 'y*--')   "
