  "body": " Adding Axis Labels   Here is an interactive code box that functions identically to the MATLAB command window.  % Try it 11.3.2 % Add a axis labels to the plot % Define the force vector force = 0:5000:40000; % Define the length vector len = [25,27,29,31.1,32.9,35,37,39,40.8]\/1000; %Calculate area based off information area = pi*0.005^2; len_0 = 0.025; %inital length %Calculate stress and strain of HDPE according to equations e_stress = force \/ area; e_strain = (len-len_0)\/len_0; %Calculate stress and strain of teflon len_teflon = [25 28.2 31.4 34.5 37.8 40.8 44.1 47.3 50.5]\/1000; e_stress_teflon = force\/area; e_strain_teflon = (len_teflon-len_0)\/len_0; % Begin Plotting % plot (e_strain, e_stress) % orginal plot command % plot (e_strain, e_stress, 'g') % plot a green line % plot (e_strain, e_stress, 'k<-.') % plot black left arrows (dashdot line) plot(e_strain,e_stress,'mp--'); % plot magenta pentagrams (dashed line) hold on plot(e_strain_teflon,e_stress_teflon,'g*--'); %any number of plotting commands can go here% hold off title('Tensile Test Data') %INSERT X AND Y LABEL HERE   "
